{pad:meta title='Service desk: how it works'/}

<div class="work-help">
  <div class="work-head">
    <div>
      <h2>Service desk, built in PAD</h2>
      <p>A support inbox with assignment, priority, handover notes, status changes and workload reports.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="work-panel">
    <h3>Try a complete workflow</h3>
    <p>Try creating a ticket, assigning it, adding a note and resolving it. Open the same ticket in two windows, save one, then save the other to see the stale-update check.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="work-panel">
    <h3>Pages</h3>
    <div class="work-table-wrap">
      <table class="work-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Page</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="?index">index</a></td>
            <td>Filter the inbox by status, priority or a literal search string.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="?new">new</a></td>
            <td>Create a validated support request.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="?reports">reports</a></td>
            <td>Read charts and a sortable workload table.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="work-panel">
    <h3>The template is the application</h3>
    <p>There are no PHP page controllers or application PHP helper libraries. Each page declares its own form rules, reads requests through PAD helpers, makes workflow decisions with PAD tags, binds database values, and renders its result. The only PHP files configure the application and enter PAD.</p>
    <pre><code>&#123;pad:if php:padPosted(&#x27;update-ticket&#x27;)&#125;
  &#123;pad:set $changed = php:db(
    &#x27;UPDATE tickets SET status=&amp;open;0&amp;close;,version=version+1 WHERE id=&amp;open;1&amp;close; AND version=&amp;open;2&amp;close;&#x27;,
    [php:padRequest(&#x27;status&#x27;),$ticketId,php:padRequest(&#x27;version&#x27;)]
  )/&#125;
&#123;/pad:if&#125;</code></pre>
    <p>Database reads use <code>pad:array</code>, <code>pad:record</code> and <code>pad:field</code>. A <code>toData</code> store connects queries to charts, tables, calendars and printables. Reusable layout slots, flash messages, fragments and the shared theme switcher complete the interface.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="work-panel">
    <h3>Data integrity</h3>
    <p>An update includes the version that the form read. If another window saves first, the old form cannot overwrite it. SQLite triggers record creation and every status, priority or assignment update in the activity history.</p>
    <p>Forms carry CSRF tokens. Literal <code>rules=</code> declarations run on the server before <code>padPosted()</code> returns true; <code>client</code> adds browser feedback from the same rules. Successful writes redirect before rendering. Search values are bound as data and output is escaped.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="work-panel">
    <h3>Storage and scope</h3>
    <p>The first visit creates <code>DATA/serviceDesk/serviceDesk.sqlite</code> from <code>apps/serviceDesk/_install/schema.sql</code>, including fictional starter records. Changes persist across visits and browser sessions. Keep that database when updating the application.</p>
    <p>This is one shared workspace for everyone who can access this installation. It does not provide user accounts or separate customer workspaces. All workflows work without application JavaScript; PAD's controls add progressive enhancements.</p>
  </section>
</div>
